{:activity/_scope [{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092995} :activity/id #uuid "95d8fd9f-fddb-5a11-8670-194ad28cdab0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049392} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092995 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093403 :tutorial/content "We know that we can write a system of three linear equations in three variables in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n- $A$ is the $3\\times 3$ coefficient matrix,\n\n- $\\mathbf{x}$ is the column vector of variables, and\n\n- $\\mathbf{b}$ is the column vector of constants.\n\nIf the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ is invertible, then we can find a solution to the system $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ by \"pre-multiplying\" both sides of the equation by $A^{-1}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ {I}_{3}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ we simply calculate $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nLet's see how this works for a particular system in the next example." :tutorial/id #uuid "4c0fe954-2cf5-5eb6-b58f-c6963f5be7f2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3054 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "8e9e60d9-ca5d-5380-9aad-e2eb767f920e" :step/math-academy-id 16484 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092996}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092996 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092185 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092025 :question/id #uuid "2737e6bc-5372-50a0-bf2f-59a91f571a57" :question/math-academy-id "e-4520" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z &=-2 \\\\ -3y+z &=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](images/22/220e8838850356768215ed74aefc469edbdc99aa50b9116729329f0e818d6978.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=3, y=0, z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=3+0+(-2)=1.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12637b1d-ca03-568f-b1fc-6a626eec88de" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049151} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "887a6a30-78e3-511e-9bc0-6c49b6d54512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091103} {:answer/id #uuid "dd686826-d59f-5882-aeab-97fbd7a6ab39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091104} {:answer/id #uuid "ea0850ba-7dfc-5a96-95c9-bd0f497d0592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091105} {:answer/id #uuid "fd58c84b-99ea-5230-baf9-e14010a02ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091106} {:answer/id #uuid "1a720563-6a6e-5f12-b22e-8a9d4be7b70b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091107}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8eeed526-fe80-58ef-9740-7cc010b25f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091102}] :question/id #uuid "53eea4a9-49d1-52f4-a825-f27d06f9350d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78548" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n${x - 2y + 4z = 7; x - y + z =-1; y - 2z =-5$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax = b$. Given that $x = ⟨x, y, z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x + y + z$?\n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n$A^{-1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be2ed44-abcd-5149-b7f8-7420617f893d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345740} {:answer/id #uuid "3d28bbd3-ecba-5dfc-b910-ddc059a2a7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345868} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa5db8e-a33a-52b0-985f-150651d6167f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345892} {:answer/id #uuid "79ef34a4-f89d-5a35-931f-34ece2d4c697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346417} {:answer/id #uuid "fcdc964c-4aad-5c08-bf12-2b64550432e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347574}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345740} :answer-field/id #uuid "02fe725a-1044-5299-8961-b4e4c4bb6218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35f6dc89-f4a6-5953-a50e-5f17ce4b6254" :question/math-academy-id "q-78557" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=2 \\\\ x-2y-5z &=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y+2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-19 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -12 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=5,y=3,z=0.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=5+3+0=8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff81d498-e200-5357-94da-1cde068c1b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291723}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291723} :answer-field/id #uuid "662aab82-835e-52a6-a86f-31ea8a24b31b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de3688b-8fa3-5a15-976c-c08362b18d73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290696}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290696} :answer-field/id #uuid "8079c99c-1a69-5aed-afe6-68e388cbfe16" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e2285e-3ebe-5d82-b306-514b4f4eb771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291048}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291048} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd3f99dc-5363-5fe9-a7f4-807e3dbcf354" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b02be14e-cb49-5b42-8e6d-3a07498cc78a" :question/math-academy-id "q-275781" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z &=-1 \\\\ x-y+3z &=2 \\\\ -2x+y-z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, and the inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe solution of the system of equations is \n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}, \n$\\,z=$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is \n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=0,\\,z=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "423263c8-910f-5e65-b0f9-72336389c763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345917} {:answer/id #uuid "4af6b490-42e2-5fbc-919a-3965e425b927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345994} {:answer/id #uuid "6d738ec6-0276-5855-9e82-cef6a4fc77a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346305} {:answer/id #uuid "79eb8b71-703e-57fb-9a19-4086912c4c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346416} {:answer/id #uuid "d6095979-6ed0-5f3a-ac81-eb469af24e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347234}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345917} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f3a74b-c665-55b0-895b-74381a508601" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "79084f5b-48d5-5007-b546-94e0eb82e68f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78421" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z &=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z &=1 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-1,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-1)+(-2)=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0646feb4-1390-58d6-b928-cb0ebf0079bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345405} {:answer/id #uuid "77f66960-d9df-5980-a7c8-aadcadf7dca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346403} {:answer/id #uuid "909f168d-0c7a-5f7d-9d7c-632172f869cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346611} {:answer/id #uuid "9e943888-4e13-5c40-9e73-cefadfb815c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346734} {:answer/id #uuid "eb30412a-7b9d-5bd3-ae57-31a7a4da9d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347425}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186346403} :answer-field/id #uuid "c29a008b-ff16-55cb-a0bf-6540d6e66731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "52850c4f-5599-59e1-a33e-81433eb41c83" :question/math-academy-id "q-78550" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-2z &=-2 \\\\ 5x+y+z &=-1 \\\\ -8x+2y+z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -13 & -15 & -11 \\\\ 18 & 22 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -13 & -15 & -11 \\\\ 18 & 22 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=4,z=-5.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+4+(-5)=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e6fad1-fc7c-5eea-9144-dc73adbf3eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345411} {:answer/id #uuid "13170d3c-ce8d-5712-974c-4dc638f5279b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345515} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d18a89-c1cb-519f-ab96-09f619a2789a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347071} {:answer/id #uuid "d9aa8796-c2f0-5e25-bec8-fb37c990ba7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347269} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e60b31-b678-5051-ba64-7b767a31a9f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347405}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345411} :answer-field/id #uuid "d571a248-b8cb-597e-b9b2-0595e78ab398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "24904e1f-067d-5336-b51d-d796d8e1a752" :question/math-academy-id "q-78551" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=1 \\\\ 3x+2y-z &=1 \\\\ x-4y+3z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-2,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f1c434-2ff5-550f-9549-1ab612ecfc54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345553} {:answer/id #uuid "2b16fd19-54ee-5c6c-b39a-2917001dba04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345733} {:answer/id #uuid "4275031c-bd68-5593-b53a-fbdeae01e2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345919} {:answer/id #uuid "604cf1e2-f619-5aad-8d53-446ef70c161d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346183} {:answer/id #uuid "d60f0776-9c63-5ad7-af58-135bcd2997bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347235}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345553} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bc6d27-6ebd-5b08-9648-ce1a14938557" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4f29a419-a479-53a4-a745-68e1440b0ad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-78554" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=0 \\\\ x+3y+z &=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y-z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $\\frac{yz}{x}?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=-1,z=3.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{yz}{x}=\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 3}{-1}=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d0c252c-7135-520f-bf91-30d61760c2b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345867} {:answer/id #uuid "53a478c0-3436-5889-8023-fed13367e6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346062} {:answer/id #uuid "b126bb4e-e277-5d67-8d38-9e42360f0690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346898} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9170e6-1cb7-53b7-b02a-ed23817c3b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346997} {:answer/id #uuid "efcf994c-b83b-5924-bda0-290dd07745d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347466}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186346898} :answer-field/id #uuid "de2d7eec-c53f-52d6-8092-de0fe5fccbb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "072e9847-9b8c-5fdc-99a1-69c9ff8518f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-78555" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-y-z &=3 \\\\ 6x-3y-5z &=5 \\\\ 5x-y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & 9 & -16 \\\\ 9 & -7 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & 9 & -16 \\\\ 9 & -7 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-5,z=2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-5)+2=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e5fd665-92c8-5de9-a962-94e1f5665e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393879} {:answer/id #uuid "b49b5346-149e-5688-b4e3-abd91ac82b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393880} {:answer/id #uuid "dde44d62-1c85-5ae3-b2b1-d15a071a6e4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393881} {:answer/id #uuid "86f61021-d77c-5497-9ea7-8d2d27863b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393882} {:answer/id #uuid "6286448b-0a3f-5139-a73d-05652685e000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393883}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393883} :answer-field/id #uuid "4352c172-b7da-52e6-b834-2727aa018a4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c98c808b-049b-59b0-8d36-61df2339933c" :question/math-academy-id "q-78549" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+4z &=-2 \\\\ x+3y+9z &=0 \\\\ y+6z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-3,z=1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-3)+1=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d740f60-2523-5646-9a92-3c0d339e8fc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393886} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f32d4d-f862-5218-b3d1-078edcdfe213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393887} {:answer/id #uuid "12eac5a8-05a9-5828-8db5-751459d1b149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393888} {:answer/id #uuid "5af9cd45-f4f1-5692-8de2-840ab3c6c7fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393889} {:answer/id #uuid "44860cb9-5129-5c07-80fe-7caff5e9aed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393890}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393887} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d59287-5dfe-56f3-93e2-54429b0c04b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "07f12953-92a4-55d6-afcb-39fb0f43a712" :question/math-academy-id "q-78552" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z &=-4 \\\\ -4x+4y-3z &=7 \\\\ x-y+z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=-1.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+2+(-1)=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc306a8-65be-5769-9f23-972df29a47cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435135} {:answer/id #uuid "b90c4ae0-c1ef-52b6-b3de-1cbcb9e94c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435139} {:answer/id #uuid "d60be700-46fb-5903-a3f8-cfb1794eaf06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435140} {:answer/id #uuid "ed96fe73-34bc-5554-8fe0-b110d7f3f6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435142} {:answer/id #uuid "f3dc6b18-74c4-595b-92c7-e48fa955a38e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435142} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e50419-c826-5a89-9337-910bb9a469c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e321af2f-d67a-5dc4-a077-c6060845ea99" :question/math-academy-id "q-78553" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z &=3 \\\\ x-2y+z &=1 \\\\ 2x-y+2z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=1,z=4.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=-1+1+4=4.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Given the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "e317b6ac-3382-5ce2-962a-936c0a5dc928" :step/math-academy-id 16485 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092997}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092997 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092186 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092026 :question/id #uuid "d32f2604-fc3f-5e80-8085-483e6fd9a3ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-4521" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z &=0 \\\\ z+4y-5 &=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z &=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z &=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e816a0fcde823bc6f6e88dff0a02c1877275cbed75757c1eb366fb224629127e.svg)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/be/beb80ea3185fc723c294313b63274554ec8af3531ed5643173a6127c59a21bb3.svg)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/e6/e6fac5dd0a9918a03ce7c14e9cd05a06c6d11e95346f261ec75d6ebea09de1d6.svg)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](images/72/72b9d627d372d7a64a271b555b0d4cbb89b2bf9d602cdec64b1d8987a5e21521.svg)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049043}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1c5547-1ac6-53d1-b475-3c1f3a7a7421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327355} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9bc47f-e4a1-5a48-ad95-9fdc8c30c725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328727} {:answer/id #uuid "e561604b-c400-5b31-b7b4-38788bbd36a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328943} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8db0ff-6f78-5797-8626-bb072f3b6837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329018} {:answer/id #uuid "ef36cb4d-9cd4-585e-b2e1-dfd00cf7e9a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329023}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327355} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8241441-5d37-5b80-8d02-80f7b14d12b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "be9d95c2-a710-5571-987b-8cd6ddd0d0ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-42449" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3+z &=0 \\\\ 5y-1+3x &=2z+1 \\\\ 3z+2x-1 &=2y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+z &=3 \\\\ 3x+5y-2z &=2 \\\\ 2x-2y+3z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-0+\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(15-4)+(-6-10) \\\\  & =22-16 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 13 & -16 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -13 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -30\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=4-4-5=-5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32a629f7-cdad-5e40-a7af-57d44a79f15c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358203} {:answer/id #uuid "97b406c3-436c-57d8-91d8-6a6d532f277b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=42,y=35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359081} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe4c40c-106e-5783-9379-eb17253bb71e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-42,y=-35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359384} {:answer/id #uuid "da2241a8-e247-5ffa-bffa-9d28c1845cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359661} {:answer/id #uuid "edfac0cb-1146-5514-b6e8-174d46a416bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=22,y=-45,z=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359871}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359661} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fa87ff7-4613-5f53-9da8-db784a9b17ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e2cd33f-1df6-521c-a13d-e818a65472f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-9722" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z+x &=-1 \\\\ 4z+y &=1 \\\\ 5x+6y-3 &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z &=-1 \\\\ y+4z &=1 \\\\ 5x+6y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-24)-2(-20)+3(-5) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & -20 & -5 \\\\ -18 & -15 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 20 & -5 \\\\ 18 & -15 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & 18 & 5 \\\\ 20 & -15 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}42 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=42,y=-35,z=9.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0737fd5b-96ea-5473-a44f-a41afd6c1553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=13,\\,y=25,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235846} {:answer/id #uuid "4537e0a4-37b3-5f1d-9fed-26057698bace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236260} {:answer/id #uuid "a124349e-3884-56ce-9385-08f24fa6a176" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=13,\\,y=19,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236824} {:answer/id #uuid "aad0b275-3680-5a33-969f-268cb505c79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11,\\,y=19,\\,z=77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236897} {:answer/id #uuid "cf542f7a-ea1a-583f-908a-f1953ea01648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-13,\\,y=19,\\,z=57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236260} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4836e15-142a-5dba-b682-0f201894c5b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "062c7a4a-d791-5879-9bf4-0c469a15394c" :question/math-academy-id "q-10038" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z+2y+7x &=1 \\\\ 3y-z &=-2 \\\\ 4y-2z-3x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+2y+z &=1 \\\\ 3y-z &=-2 \\\\ -3x+4y-2z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =7\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =7(-6+4)-2(-3)+1(9) \\\\  & =-14+6+9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 9 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 34 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -34 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 77\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-18,\\,y=25,\\,z=77.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f4398f-18db-5bb4-ab9f-e4e728621f7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235973} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7a6fdc-7ce6-5e15-89a2-84e59db68519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236221} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1cb93d-039d-5852-a40e-003b41fbe609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-30,y=-20,z=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236697} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c46c33-108b-5ebb-8533-fcb6694cba67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237004} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1a6c04-3807-5923-9a4c-3658958aaca1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-15,y=-10,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235973} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f2b74e1-36cd-50e9-b37c-03195ff066d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a8a38c1-8d83-5c15-8052-a8f7706f20a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-10074" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z &=-1-x \\\\ 4y &=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z &=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z &=0 \\\\ x+6z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18cf84eb-8019-5024-a9d4-f6d05cfd3269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=19,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235970} {:answer/id #uuid "4f20d1b9-9c63-50d2-a24e-b400decf2a29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236328} {:answer/id #uuid "5b847704-0397-5367-962e-626db03c9d3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,y=\\frac{19}{5},z=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236389} {:answer/id #uuid "b802e7d8-4eb2-58b7-9ef0-5acd50e6d76a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236989} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d25859-b8ae-5dba-8a88-d56b4edbf4be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=-19,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237083}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236989} :answer-field/id #uuid "46b1f130-63be-5d63-8f37-389b677d9647" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e779cc8b-bc48-5f02-aa7a-6ab946e667e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-10075" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3z-y+x-5 &=0 \\\\ y+2x+2z &=1 \\\\ z-2x-2y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z &=5 \\\\ 2x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ -2x-2y+z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1+4)+1(2+4)+3(-4+2) \\\\  & =5+6-6 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -\\frac{19}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=3,y=-\\frac{19}{5},z=-\\frac{3}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338ad7db-610c-5504-8b07-93ddf6989bc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236141} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb5824f-641f-50ba-a60c-6f273e5bc745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-19,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236307} {:answer/id #uuid "87dae3e4-1d42-58e8-97db-0124534b5c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=42,y=-35,z=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236665} {:answer/id #uuid "f5dd7272-ba74-59ef-a368-6470a994b20e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=15,y=-49,z=-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237366} {:answer/id #uuid "f757ba64-10e8-5058-8e1b-0c55eb97642d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=19,y=49,z=58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236141} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd21ae35-d429-561d-927c-fa4d44ff854e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e8e08af1-fca9-5664-99a6-119c31e3f669" :question/math-academy-id "q-10076" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z &=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z &=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4128ba71-30f4-5d9f-a1da-f0feb798ee82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-29,y=-12,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236233} {:answer/id #uuid "4a578053-2e19-50df-9af8-8b315860043c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-29,y=-12,z=-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236294} {:answer/id #uuid "5c4620a0-76d3-5e9f-92c3-382dca21ee9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=29,y=12,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236392} {:answer/id #uuid "88066dff-8cdf-5893-a4d3-81d269f7ee2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-25,y=-12,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236666} {:answer/id #uuid "b8391916-39bd-5633-8b71-eb03b0decc7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-29,y=-15,z=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236233} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7b3d13-f904-586b-ba35-a7c8c21f7369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c7f748e9-7cb4-573b-a324-159e0e3861ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-10100" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z &=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z &=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(7-2)-3(-2)+1(4-21) \\\\  & =10+6-17 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & -17 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -17 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -17 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -17 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 17 & -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 17 & -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-29 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 100\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-29,y=-12,z=100.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee7e0cc-1841-50f3-a5f2-a54b57df7f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8,y=-8,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236414} {:answer/id #uuid "79759bba-4475-51ba-874e-be7acc9f35b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236581} {:answer/id #uuid "e806513b-a961-5fd9-b571-b43cd8457290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3},y=\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237278} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd5388f-1f93-52d6-b413-aa7b0e4d018d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8,y=8,z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237302} {:answer/id #uuid "fd42bafb-20e3-522c-919b-8c6a78d5d018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186236581} :answer-field/id #uuid "3334def8-af8d-5c3c-8b52-9e05eccf839f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a8cc406f-67fe-55bc-b55e-b6858ce9be1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-10101" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(1-3(-2))+0-1(-2-3) \\\\  & =1+6+2+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=\\frac{2}{3},y=-\\frac{2}{3},z=\\frac{2}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "432a51a6-a859-539f-aad3-0c3afb4b46f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236251} {:answer/id #uuid "95ab3dfc-0bd9-5c63-b32d-b78ab929c832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=-4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236768} {:answer/id #uuid "c356000e-035d-577e-85f1-5fd545858205" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237051} {:answer/id #uuid "c3eca95b-b2df-58cc-bfa3-67df1d256020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,y=8,z=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237054} {:answer/id #uuid "ed9f0f71-f5a0-5bca-9a3b-a6ddd72eabaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5,y=8,z=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237316}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237051} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7f236a0-c448-555c-b80c-c66d10276c27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "267865d4-e8c6-50f1-8813-4866781fbd07" :question/math-academy-id "q-10102" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+2z &=1 \\\\ x+y+z &=3 \\\\ y+2z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-2(2)+2(1) \\\\  & =-4+2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=\\frac{5}{2},y=4,z=-\\frac{7}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290df338-cbf5-5bde-98fe-bac5fcf6883e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238418} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddc03a9-31e0-5513-b8a2-708a0189a34d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239146} {:answer/id #uuid "8c16ab80-c07b-5b4b-ad79-83a262db83fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239272} {:answer/id #uuid "b62a8c7a-d543-5087-9732-2e1cdd0bd83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239645} {:answer/id #uuid "e537f447-3bfe-5af5-84c5-e2af277694e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240067}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240067} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbcab08-178c-57a6-a96a-3ec75b0b9a67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b86d16b9-91e7-5d11-97b1-e0f931afe9d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-104536" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+z &=1 \\\\ 2x-2z &=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z &=2x-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+z &=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z &=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1604f16b-b6ec-5977-8db2-4745c554c4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,y=-11,z=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238242} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd6c920-44cd-558c-b5b5-5a4fb709b7fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11,y=6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238330} {:answer/id #uuid "37255593-62a2-5d88-b4ca-46ad8477c825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=6,z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238534} {:answer/id #uuid "862e6d9d-6938-55b2-9966-6d4c843929b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239222} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e74476-4ff0-5e8b-8dc3-25b96e048393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6,y=-3,z=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239222} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d168cf8-68f1-5703-91a1-1c3db1aa2a7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "30372d4a-7cb0-560b-a8cf-a404cabf96f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-104541" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x &=2 \\\\ -3z+y &=3 \\\\ 2x+y &=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=2 \\\\ y-3z &=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef491d6-2ab5-50e3-af24-150a984cf7e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1,y=2,z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238315} {:answer/id #uuid "6433840e-f62b-5d25-8771-780117ffbb37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1,y=1,z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238933} {:answer/id #uuid "7d19c17c-f45c-59ab-ad2c-fc3a4aac1a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1,y=-2,z=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239137} {:answer/id #uuid "e38fd3ea-ff34-57f1-b478-4bbf6667b49b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,y=-1,z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240056} {:answer/id #uuid "e8758369-817b-5292-aa34-f56b3a84956f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2,y=1,z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240101}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238315} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3164e39-ba71-5ae7-8548-2f22c8c3ac60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5c5fa419-7d88-586a-9224-2f097b998fb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104546" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z+x &=2 \\\\ 2y-3z &=1 \\\\ 2z-y &=-3x+3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=2 \\\\ 2y-3z &=1 \\\\ 3x-y+2z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4-3)-0+(0-6) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=1,y=2,z=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a3fe0d-b34c-5bb8-b1f3-dc5d8eca2468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290720} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e2a83e-a1a8-5c12-9edf-33f4a344c96c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6634bf9f-785d-5998-8bc6-6bf2bf22b822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291066}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291066} :answer-field/id #uuid "93a02cdf-28be-5434-93d5-c6e111efd86d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292197} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fec0e11e-aa0a-549e-b6fc-7edf5f309577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291721}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291721} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1d42cae-af03-514c-b698-ac6e1baf7763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b1472133-fedd-5702-9754-ac7f5c7dd85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-275787" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=4x+y+2 \\\\ x+y &=2z+2 \\\\ y &=x-y+z+1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x-y+z &=2 \\\\ x+y-2z &=2 \\\\ -x+2y-z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3(-1+4)+(-1-2)+(2+1) \\\\  & =-9-3+3 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "546c8e95-b26b-5ff9-83d6-638b399b687a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415684} {:answer/id #uuid "854c87f7-583e-578a-92c5-d3db59792427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415685} {:answer/id #uuid "92176233-f61a-5a1f-a96a-0e59d129daf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=-9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415686} {:answer/id #uuid "922397fb-a6df-5cdc-b3c4-40ed001f749e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,y=18,z=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415687} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d344f8-2327-5d63-96e1-0bdf947cb05c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,y=-18,z=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415684} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7180735-62b0-5917-9dd2-0f45d066402b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2997dd93-b478-5bad-935c-182c80540138" :question/math-academy-id "q-10091" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-1(1-9)+2(1-6) \\\\  & =+8-10 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 9 \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039d5f33-dfa0-51c2-93be-2b7000137d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435129} {:answer/id #uuid "0597b830-4974-5289-8d3c-e5ddb2d894f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435130} {:answer/id #uuid "274c794a-3cbb-5dc2-bbb2-1f1131f70f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435131} {:answer/id #uuid "28126022-8f20-5f62-8417-0685db76f23b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435132} {:answer/id #uuid "3b9511ec-b4f9-5c7b-b596-beebd0bcb054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435134}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435132} :answer-field/id #uuid "d554649a-905d-57c6-af27-cc40c4c45a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0807a9e2-ba3b-5d6e-8562-a580bc61f62a" :question/math-academy-id "q-104515" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z &=-1 \\\\ 3x-z &=5+3y \\\\ 3z-2y &=6-x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z &=-1 \\\\ 3x-3y-z &=5 \\\\ x-2y+3z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-9-2)-(9+1)-2(-6+3) \\\\  & =-22-10+6 \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}-26 \\\\ 26 \\\\ -26\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=1-1+1=1.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "fbf465d4-96d6-52f9-879f-09f247f27b80" :step/math-academy-id 16486 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092999}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092999 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092187 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092027 :question/id #uuid "06a50eb4-4976-55fd-aa44-6509b27eccb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4604" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d},$ where $A$ and $B$ are $10 \\times 10$ non-singular matrices, while $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ are $10 \\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $\\mathbf{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse $B^{−1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,\\mathbf{x} = A^{-1}\\,\\mathbf{d}$ by $B^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{10}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6772684b-7ff9-55af-9868-58a570196839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${I}_{3}$ and ${D}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346253} {:answer/id #uuid "6974c2e1-ba12-5b9a-aeea-f561962b4665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ and $D$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346266} {:answer/id #uuid "9a10c769-4cd4-5a72-b2b1-b6ff7374a605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346696} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fa6559-c5e3-577c-9d7a-11da3b40b6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ and ${I}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346820} {:answer/id #uuid "ba1448e4-477d-5544-9da4-da383a58e2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ and ${D}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186346696} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ef4bdad-d808-5e35-aada-a2a7a44b3522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "15bdd24c-e192-58dc-b8c4-b4c9d91ba43f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78442" :question/problem "Consider a system of $3$ linear equations in $3$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,y=w.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $y$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $w$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w \\\\  & ={D}^{-1}\\,w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,y=w$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,y & =w \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,y & ={D}^{-1}w \\\\ {I}_{3}\\,y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w \\\\ y & ={D}^{-1}\\,w\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $y.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30508e44-d4cb-59cd-b6e2-9a9a1a4b255d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345780} {:answer/id #uuid "6c7096ce-24dc-566e-8c30-db63da01af3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346291} {:answer/id #uuid "8cbe8157-e1ae-5842-9999-a076c2effff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346576} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8fbf04-654a-5fa0-bc5f-6c071e032cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}A\\,d" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346599} {:answer/id #uuid "ab98b004-bd42-5343-bd83-320ee30a060c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345780} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef8ff4f-63f9-5ee0-ab75-109802dee162" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "85f32905-fc93-542c-bb5c-0482b0afbff9" :question/math-academy-id "q-78572" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299656 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b613db7-3639-5cfa-8355-3eda8dde4a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Ab" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297671} {:answer/id #uuid "2d07001d-219e-5a54-8e7b-a8e55434a3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297742} {:answer/id #uuid "51acb5a0-36e9-5e3d-9c37-06230f28f670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "bA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297897} {:answer/id #uuid "8be8e53b-8e70-5d31-b2d7-9a5de3c0f54c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298159}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297742} :answer-field/id #uuid "aecff7e3-afce-52e5-acb9-05ee2422ca92" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29445ea8-6882-5534-9d88-5e8b0cf3e66e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answ